WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:13.721
Will the weather hold today? Smoke's going straight up. No wind, no rain. We'll get the corn in.

2
00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:19.992
Heads only, mind. Cut them high. Leave the straw standing for the cattle.

3
00:00:32.494 --> 00:00:36.921
The boy's bringing the cattle up off the marsh, before the big tides come.

4
00:00:37.494 --> 00:00:43.985
Good. Last autumn the water came over the marsh in the night, and we lost a calf.

5
00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:51.063
Not this year. The pig's fat, the store's full, and the cloth's nearly done for the little one's cloak.

6
00:00:57.764 --> 00:01:05.364
Listen, little one. Geese, going over. The cold's coming. Bring wood in by the door tonight.

7
00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:12.412
And before dark, a handful of the new corn goes down to the spring. It has always given us water.

8
00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:29.181
See the smoke over the brow? They've the fires lit up at the stone house already. Good spelt this year. Dry enough to thresh before the rain comes up the valley.

9
00:01:30.084 --> 00:01:39.945
Then thresh it quick. The quern's hungry, and so are the children. Fine red pots from far off, and we still eat the same porridge out of them.

10
00:01:46.644 --> 00:01:57.244
Call them in, then. There's cloud coming up off the marsh. And the geese are fat this year: one for the turn of the year, and one for your mother, or we'll never hear the end of it.

11
00:01:57.644 --> 00:02:01.026
Let them run. The hill's big enough for all of us.

